{"name":"Gun Powder","hex":"#484753","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"gun powder","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of gunpowder."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gun_powder"}],"entries":[{"title":"Gunpowder","blocks":[{"text":"Gunpowder, referred to as black powder to distinguish it from modern smokeless powder, is the earliest known chemical explosive. It consists of a mixture of sulfur, charcoal, and potassium nitrate (saltpeter). The sulfur and charcoal act as fuels, while the saltpeter is an oxidizer. Gunpowder has been widely used as a propellant in firearms, artillery, rocketry, and pyrotechnics, including use as a blasting agent for explosives in quarrying, mining, building pipelines, tunnels, and roads."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Black_Powder-1.JPG/330px-Black_Powder-1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gunpowder","wikidata":"Q12861"},{"title":"Gun","blocks":[{"text":"A gun is a device that propels a projectile using pressure or explosive force. The projectiles are typically solid, but can also be pressurized liquid, or gas. Solid projectiles may be free-flying or tethered. A large-caliber gun is also called a cannon, while a hand-held gun may be called a firearm. Guns were designed as weapons for military use, and then found use in hunting."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/SIG_Pro_by_Augustas_Didzgalvis.jpg/330px-SIG_Pro_by_Augustas_Didzgalvis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gun","wikidata":"Q110155210"},{"title":"Powder","blocks":[{"text":"A powder is a dry solid composed of many very fine particles that may flow freely when shaken or tilted. Powders are a special sub-class of granular materials, although the terms powder and granular are sometimes used to distinguish separate classes of material. In particular, powders refer to those granular materials that have the finer grain sizes, and that therefore have a greater tendency to form clumps when flowing. Granulars refer to the coarser granular materials that do not tend to form clumps except when wet."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Iron_powder.JPG/330px-Iron_powder.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Powder","wikidata":"Q2908004"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Veterans_Weekend%2C_Hull_-_panoramio.jpg/500px-Veterans_Weekend%2C_Hull_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Veterans_Weekend%2C_Hull_-_panoramio.jpg/500px-Veterans_Weekend%2C_Hull_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"American Civil War re-enactors volley firing with black powder","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVeterans_Weekend%2C_Hull_-_panoramio.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Z%C3%BCndkraut_mit_Z%C3%BCndkrautspender.jpg/500px-Z%C3%BCndkraut_mit_Z%C3%BCndkrautspender.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Z%C3%BCndkraut_mit_Z%C3%BCndkrautspender.jpg/1280px-Z%C3%BCndkraut_mit_Z%C3%BCndkrautspender.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Z%C3%BCndkraut_mit_Z%C3%BCndkrautspender.jpg/500px-Z%C3%BCndkraut_mit_Z%C3%BCndkrautspender.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Flash pan starter dispenser","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AZ%C3%BCndkraut_mit_Z%C3%BCndkrautspender.jpg"},{"sr